{
  "$comment": "EXP-1291 Threads v2: the THREAD screen ×4 (a thread IS a root session). Header = the title + ONE tab strip: Conversation · one issue chip per linked issue (session_issues of the ROOT by sortOrder; unsynced issues drop out) · '+' (link/file an issue; ALWAYS right after the issue chips) · the session chips (EXP-1316, below) · Guide (a dot while the root's guide holds any text or picture); nothing else (no captions, no Stop, no right sidebar). Phones use the strip as the pager. Conversation rows = the root's own session card first (session-card.json, ordinal 1), then the ROOT's messages oldest first (createdAt, ties by id): a card-less row = a message bubble (author user|agent|system, empty bodies skipped; a person's row reads `queued` until the device consumed it); card `session`/`thread_started` = that session's card (ordinal = its place in the tree's creation order; an unsynced target drops out); `question` (question, options, answer, answered = answeredAt set) and `plan` (plan, decision) answer IN the card; `subagent` (title, status); `picture` (attachmentId, width, height, caption; no attachmentId = dropped); `event` = one muted line from `copy.events` ({issue} = the issue's identifier, {pr} = '#<number>'; an unresolvable target or unknown event = dropped); unknown card kinds are dropped. Children's own messages never inline: they show when that session is opened. The composer below = THE session composer box (Composer primitive), placeholder `copy.placeholder`, sending `sessions.send({sessionId: root})` (an ended thread continues server-side in a new child). title = threadTitle (EXP-1316, nobody renames a thread ×4, no `sessions.setTitle`): kind agent → its `name`; else an action → `titles.action` (`Run <action name>`); else linked issues (the root's SYNCED issues by sortOrder) → `titles.issue` (`Implement EXP-12`), with n>1 `titles.issues` (`Implement EXP-12 + <n-1>`), plain text, no pill; else the stored title (the CLI's auto-name, written by `sessions.report` only while blank; the engine asks for it only on pure chats: no issues, no action); else the first line of the root's first person message (image lines skipped, capped at `titleMax` chars with '…'); else `copy.untitled`. The server's `deriveSessionTitle` = the same function. private = !root.shared (a lock glyph beside the title). live/busy/needsYou aggregate the tree's non-ended sessions. Model = pure `buildSessionThread(input)` (packages/domain-contract/src/session-tree.ts), every mirror replays `cases` comparing the WHOLE expected object. EXP-1306 (owner 2026-10-14): the GUIDE tab ×4 = the root's Guide text over ONE pull request, `guidePullRequest(pullRequests)` (the root's pull_requests; every mirror replays `guidePullRequestCases`): the newest OPEN one (createdAt, ties by the higher number), else the newest MERGED one, else none (a closed PR never counts). When that PR sits in a linear open stack (pr-stack-view.json `stackView` over the repository's pull requests: head = branch, base = prBaseBranch) a `copy.stack` band (the pr-stack glyph, no count) + THE StackRail (top first, the PR's row = the current wash, down to its base branch; a row opens that PR's thread, the hovered/long-pressed row offers Merge through here) leads the Guide; no stack = no block. NO pull-request rows, no inline Merge, no Pull requests band. While the PR is open THE white bottom Merge capsule closes the tab (`testIds.guideMerge`; `Merge stack` on an open-stack member, the one stack confirm). The SESSION view (a session card opens it): while a question or plan card waits on the viewer the CARD takes the composer's place (EXP-820) ×4, the composer leaves and its draft comes back with it: `composerYieldsToCard({live, pendingAsk})` = live AND an unanswered question/plan the viewer may answer; every mirror replays `composerCases`. EXP-1307 (2026-10-14): Open on GitHub + Close PR live in ONE `…` (ui-more) in the thread HEADER's trailing slot ×4 (web/desktop: the title row's end; phones: the header's action slot), shown only while the Guide tab is showing and the Guide has a PR (`guidePullRequest`); `testIds.guideMenu` = the trigger. Its entries = `guideMenuEntries({state, member})` (state = that PR's state, null = no PR; every mirror replays `guideMenuCases`): `open-github` (contract diffUi.openOnGithub, the ui-github glyph) always, then `close-pr` (close-pr.json menuItem, pr-closed glyph, destructive) while the PR is open and the viewer is a member; Close confirms with close-pr.json's dialog (batchLine when the PR links other issues). Empty = no trigger. The bottom capsule stays Merge alone. EXP-1316 session chips: `tabs` carries `{kind: 'session', sessionId, name, markState}` after `add` and before `guide` = the sessions at the VIEWED level: on the thread = the root's own run, then its DIRECT children (tree creation order, createdAt then id); with `buildSessionThread(input, {focus})` (cases carry `options.focus`) = that session first (the active chip), then ITS direct children; nothing deeper. `focusId` = the focused session (null = the thread). name = sessionCard's name (stored title, else `Session N` by tree ordinal); markState = sessionTabMarkState = threadRowMarkState({needsYou, busy}) of THAT session, `ended` once it ended. Every chip in the strip is ONE height (entity-chip.json tab size). Clicking a session chip or a session card opens the session IN PLACE on web md+ and the IDE (`?tab=session&session=<id>` on the thread route; `/sessions/$sessionId` stays a redirect for deep links): the header + strip stay, the body = the raw work, the header's trailing slot gains its Stop pill while live; phones keep pushing the session screen (own back header). Hover (md+/IDE) or long-press (phones) on the session group = the tree popover (list-item.json SessionRow small rows + TreeGuides, the whole tree, the current row washed). EXP-1316 embedded issue: the issue tab = the issue body WITHOUT its own header bar, mobile header, Threads row, Start control or pin (title row, properties, description, files, relations, activity + comments stay; the phone bottom bar keeps properties + Comment only). EXP-1316 phone header: the thread screen wears detail-chrome.json's header band (blur + scrim + edge fade, content scrolls under it): `‹` · the title on ONE line (not tappable) + the lock · `…`, the strip (the pager) inside the band. Phones' reply box = THE floating composer capsule (collapsed: a capsule reading `copy.placeholder` floating over the content above the bottom edge fade; tap expands it into THE Composer card: text, + images/files, send, Stop while busy; collapses on blur), the session view uses the same component; web md+/IDE keep the in-flow Composer box. EXP-1316 header merge (amends EXP-1306/1307 on web md+ and the IDE): while `guidePullRequest` is open the header's trailing slot = the Merge pill (`Merge PR` | `Merge stack`), then the Stop pill while the focused session is live, then the `…` on EVERY tab (not only the Guide); phones keep the white bottom Merge capsule on the Guide tab. EXP-1316 one card: `question` and `plan` rows render THE session view's card ×4 (the same component and answer path, `sessions.answer`): a question offers its options AND a free-text answer (`custom: true`; `answer` may be any string, not only an option), a plan its decision + note; the thread draws no reduced card of its own. An answered card renders CLOSED (chosen answer / decision shown, options inert) on every client whichever path answered it: the thread card (`sessions.answer`) or the session view (relay → device → `sessions.resolveCard`). `sessions.resolveCard({messageId, answer?, decision?, feedback?})` = the DEVICE's write-back (its owner's token, the same steer auth as `answer`): stamps the same answered `card` + `answeredAt` while still null, `{ok: true}` idempotently when already answered (never CONFLICT), and enqueues nothing: the engine resolved that question itself, so the card left the engine's open cards (`outbox.resolve_question`) and the pickup, which only feeds answered cards still OPEN in the engine, never re-feeds it. EXP-1317 queue: a person's OWN queued row (queued = true, authorId = the viewer) carries ONE `Remove from queue` X ×4 (the ui-close glyph, tooltip `Remove from queue`, `sessions.unqueue`); its tooltip never outlives the button (the IDE keys the button on (message id, queued) and drops the tooltip when the row flips).",
